Write the full script from that outline. Follow the guide's format exactly.

Start with the `# Characters` section, then `# Scenes`, then `# Script` — in that order. Include every character who speaks or takes action, and every unique location.

- Action lines: plain, present-tense, physical. No adjectives piled up. No emotional narration.
- Dialogue: short, natural, how people actually talk. Avoid speeches.
- Show things happening — don't tell us what characters feel.
- One SHOT note per scene, 1-2 sentences, describing only what's specific to this scene.
- No preamble before the Characters section.
